# Worker Rules

- **Local Worker Runtime**: Run orchestration inside a local Node.js process (`worker/`) until Phase V1-A7 Vercel Workflows migration.
- **Interval Management**:
  - Health loop: execute session health checks on a 30-minute interval (`healthLoop.js`).
  - Scrape loop: execute job scrapers on a daily scheduled interval (`scrapeLoop.js`).
  - Apply loop: continuous sequential queue processing (`applyLoop.js`).
- **Sequential Execution**: Process jobs strictly one at a time per session; never run parallel application jobs.
- **Atomic Claiming**: Always claim next pending job via atomic `claim_next_job` Postgres RPC function.
- **Rate Limit Check**: Check and increment the 300 actions/day limit via `checkAndIncrementActionCount` before executing bot jobs.
- **Stub / Real Function Wiring**:
  - Encapsulate all Side B bot functions behind clean interface imports (`sideB.js`).
  - Use stubs during development; wire real bot functions once Phase checkpoints pass without altering loop orchestration logic.
